  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「オリザ・ルフィポゴン」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%83%AA%E3%82%B6%E3%83%BB%E3%83%AB%E3%83%95%E3%82%A3%E3%83%9D%E3%82%B4%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110444309,
      "text": "オリザ・ルフィポゴン は、イネ科イネ属の植物である。和名はノイネあるいはヒゲナガノイネ、英語では「weedy red rice」「brownbeard rice」などと呼ばれ、中国語では「普通野生稲」と呼ばれている。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Oryza rufipogon」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryza_rufipogon",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1360715348,
      "text": "Oryza rufipogon is a species of flowering plant in the family Poaceae. It is known as brownbeard rice, wild rice, and red rice. In 1965, Oryza nivara was separated off from O. rufipogon. The separation has been questioned, and now many sources consider O. nivara to be a synonym of O. rufipogon. O. nivara may be treated as the annual form of O. rufipogon."
    }
  },
